# Playwright

Use `@playwright/test`. Rely on auto-waiting and web-first assertions. Tests must be independent and parallel-safe.

Do not use `waitForTimeout()` unless the reason is documented in code as unavoidable.

Assertions belong in tests (or a named validator). Assert business outcomes, not DOM trivia.

Configure (when scaffolding): HTML report, screenshot on failure, trace on failure/retry. Do not add custom logging until it helps debug CI failures.

```typescript
// ✅
await expect(candidatePage.successMessage).toBeVisible();

// ❌
await page.waitForTimeout(5000);
expect(await page.locator('div:nth-child(4)').count()).toBe(1);
```
